      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I opened a canny about this, not realizing this is ultimately the same issue with further testing.\n\nThis appears to occur when you're in Temporary Pose Space. This could mean using GoGoLoco poses or ultimately, as this canny mentions, Set Horizon Adjust.\n\nThe issue is reproduced when another player **switched** into a **newly** loaded avatar, as in it has the \"Unpacking...\" status for you before loading. (Avatars of players joining a world, being hidden and shown, or avatars other players recently loaded into, do not affect you.)\n\nOR\n\nWhen another player changes their avatar height/size on any avatar.\n\nBoth of these appears to cause your temporary pose space to retrigger, which will cause the viewpoint to reset.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
