      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I just realized what the issue is, I'm still experiencing this but only within a range around when my head is 'supposed' to be. If I playspace drag low or high enough the issue doesn't tend to occur. This is still really frustrating cause this range is still a solid meter or so and I often want to playspace drag less than this while horizon adjusted.\n\nThough rarely this isn't true at all and it happens regardless of range, and sometimes it just doesn't happen at all for the duration I'm in a world?\n\nIf someone on the VRC team wants to continue regressing this issue, here are the avatar IDs that still run into this very consistently on my end:\n\n- avtr_0ae49d76-b531-494a-aa77-7c2bbbf8221d\n\n- avtr_da85e1da-3954-4a3d-8102-f4e0f1c3cd8d\n\notherwise, I'll make a new canny post if this is deemed a separate issue. Though to be fair the behaviour described is identical, I just don't think it was fully fixed.",
